# Ocentra Parent Universal Logging and Redaction Rules

This rule is universal. It is not Cloudflare-only.

Any new or edited runtime, service, domain behavior, app command path, proof helper, test, script, or Rust crate involved in a command/event/request/read-model chain must be logger-ready unless it is pure schema, constants, brands, generated data, or static docs.

## Required detailed pattern

Read:

- `docs/repo-audits/event-driven-proof-architecture/LOGGER_USAGE_PATTERN_STANDARD.md`
- `docs/repo-audits/event-driven-proof-architecture/LOGGED_PROOF_CHAIN_STANDARD.md`

## Structured Logs Only

- Use `@ocentra-parent/logging-domain` for TypeScript log shapes and logger/test-log/app-log/bridge surfaces.
- Use `crates/ocentra-eventing` event/journal/request/replay surfaces for Rust runtime proof chains where applicable.
- Do not add raw console logging in app/runtime/proof code.
- Do not invent log fields at call sites.
- Do not add a second logging system.

## Logger-ready source rule

New or edited core chain files should initialize the logger pattern from `LOGGER_USAGE_PATTERN_STANDARD.md`.

Use it in:

- packages with runtime/domain behavior;
- app/portal command paths and dev proof routes;
- scripts and proof runners;
- tests proving command/event chains;
- infra handlers/workers when present;
- Rust crates through a Rust parity trace/event adapter.

Do not remove logger helpers only because they are initially unused. Add or use a narrow lint exception for the logger-ready pattern when needed.

## Controlled enablement

Runtime logging must not become noisy.

| Context | Rule |
| --- | --- |
| production | errors and selected warnings only, redacted |
| dev command route | selected chain logs enabled |
| tests | selected chain logs enabled |
| proof runners | logs required as proof artifacts |
| failed proof debug | expanded logs allowed only if scoped and redacted |

## Redaction First

Never log:

- child names
- account secrets
- auth tokens
- raw screenshots
- raw URLs from browsing activity
- full process command lines
- keystrokes
- clipboard content
- message contents

If a field might later contain sensitive activity, store a stable category, status, hash, id, or redacted summary instead.

## Diagnostics

Dev diagnostics must be useful without leaking private data:

- service version
- platform
- mode
- feature enabled flags
- correlation ids
- schema versions
- event types
- owner package/crate
- command/event/request/read-model name
- no-claim/manual-required/degraded reason

## Proof-chain rule

A passing test is not enough for cross-owner behavior. The test or proof runner must emit enough structured log/event/read-model evidence to show where the chain started, what owner handled it, what event/request was emitted, what consumer reacted, and where it stopped if it failed.

Add tests when adding log shapes, redaction behavior, or proof-chain instrumentation.
